HST Office: Word's page border art. Every one of Word's 164 names survives a DOCX opened and saved, Page Border
offers an Art list, and pages paint the art on screen, in print and in PDF.

- Word writes only the name, size and colour; it draws its own art for the name. HST draws 24 sets of its own from
  simple geometry in hstpageartsets.cxx, nothing copied or traced, and each of the 164 names maps to one of them.
- The art is kept in the page formats' grab bag. A plain line of the art's width keeps the layout, painted over by
  the art. ODF has no such element: a saved .odt keeps that plain line, and the art is lost there.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0); hstpageart* are new files, MPL-2.0.
Test: tests/runtime/check-dialogs-writer.py page-art
